  "name": "Fraud in state programs",
  "blurb": "Fraud against state-funded programs has become one of Minnesota's main 2026 issues. In an August 2026 KSTP/SurveyUSA poll, 15% of likely voters named fraud as the most important issue in the election, and 35% named inflation and the cost of living. In 2026 the Legislature created an independent state Office of the Inspector General to oversee the existing agency watchdogs and investigate fraud. The House also voted to give legislators the full, unredacted Optum review of fraud risk in Medicaid. Supporters of the new office call it overdue. Some members said it duplicates work done by the Bureau of Criminal Apprehension and the Legislative Auditor, or questioned its law-enforcement bureau.",
