  "name": "MinnesotaCare for undocumented adults",
  "blurb": "In 2023 Minnesota opened MinnesotaCare, its state-subsidized health insurance for low-income residents, to adults without legal immigration status. Ending that coverage for adults became part of the 2025 budget deal, at Republicans' insistence. The repeal passed in the June 9, 2025 special session, with one DFL vote in the House and four in the Senate. Supporters said the state pays the full cost for this group and that the money was needed elsewhere. Opponents said people would lose care and that emergency-room care costs more. Children stay eligible.",
