  "id": "taxes",
  "name": "Taxes and the cost of living",
  "blurb": "Inflation and the cost of living are the top issue for Minnesota voters: 35% of likely voters named them in the August 2026 KSTP/SurveyUSA poll. With the House tied and the Senate held by the DFL, both parties had to agree on each year's tax bill. The 2025 special-session tax bill raised the cannabis gross receipts tax and taxed data centers' electricity use. It passed the Senate by one vote. The 2026 tax bill mostly matches state law to federal tax changes. It also adds a one-time increase in homestead credit refunds, sets up a direct free filing system and puts a 100% penalty on money received through fraud of a public program. It passed both chambers by wide margins.",
